fields.description:
Algorithm select. Chooses the hash algorithm that the init command loads into the selected context.

Usage: Program it before the init command; changing it later does not change a message in progress.

Values:
0x0 SHA-224;
0x1 SHA-256 (reset value);
0x2 SHA-384;
0x3 SHA-512;
0x4 SHA-512/224;
0x5 SHA-512/256;
0x8 SHA3-224;
0x9 SHA3-256;
0xA SHA3-384;
0xB SHA3-512;
0xC SHAKE128;
0xD SHAKE256.

Unit: code

Limits: The other codes are reserved. A code whose bit is 0 in the capability register is rejected with the configuration error event.

Context state. State of the selected context.

Usage: Read it after an error to see where the message stopped.

Values:
0x0 free (reset value);
0x1 absorbing message words;
0x2 padding and last blocks;
0x3 digest ready;
0x4 squeezing output (SHAKE);
0xF locked by a fault.

Unit: none

Limits: none

Error kind. Kind of the latest window error.

Usage: Read after an overflow, underflow, AXI or length event.

Values:
0x0 no error (reset value);
0x1 write to a full input window dropped;
0x2 read of an empty output window returned zero;
0x3 access to the wrong window direction;
0x4 unsupported AXI transaction rejected with SLVERR;
0x5 message length limit exceeded.

Unit: none

Limits: none
